      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Rice grows in diverse conditions, from deeply flooded fields to dry, hilly uplands; flooding is common in cultivation but not essential.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://ricetoday.irri.org/rice-domestication/",
        "https://herbaria.plants.ox.ac.uk/bol/plants400/Profiles/OP/Oryza"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indica rice is commonly associated with long, non-sticky grains and tropical lowlands; japonica is associated with stickier grains and temperate or upland settings.",
